# Double Check - Cursor Rules

Always reference @double-check-prd.md for feature scope and behavior.
If a request conflicts with the PRD, flag it before writing code.

## Brand
- Name: Double Check
- Tone: Meticulous and Premium
- Voice in UI copy: declarative, concise, confident

## Design Language
- Apple minimalism: prioritize whitespace, bold typography, and smooth transitions.
- Background must be pure black (#000000). Foreground must be pure white (#FFFFFF).
- Do not introduce gray colors except a very subtle border token.
- Typography should use Inter from next/font.
- Use Framer Motion for interaction and section transitions.

## Criteria System
- Keep criteria in a single typed source of truth (for example: src/lib/criteria.ts).
- Each criterion must include: id, label, negativePrompt.
- Gemini prompts must be assembled from active criteria negativePrompt values.
- Do not hardcode dietary logic inside UI components.
- Initial standards must include: Vegan, Kosher, No Meat, No Dairy, No Peanuts, No Shellfish, No Gluten.

## Labor Illusion
- Every scan interaction must take at least 2500ms before verdict display.
- Status messages must follow this exact order:
  1. Ingesting menu data...
  2. Applying your exact standards...
  3. Hunting for hidden non-compliances...
  4. Verifying culinary integrity...
  5. Selection curated.
- Display one status message at a time with cross-fade transitions.

## Stack and conventions
- Next.js App Router + Tailwind CSS + Shadcn UI + Framer Motion.
- TypeScript strict mode; avoid any.
- Server Components by default; use "use client" only where interaction is required.
